menu "BYOK hardware unknowns (RE placeholders, hw_config.h Sec.13)"

    # BYOK_HW_BATT_DIVIDER_RATIO_X1000 and BYOK_HW_CHARGER_STAT_POLARITY used
    # to live here as guessed placeholders. Both were resolved CONFIRMED
    # from the stock image's own readBatteryVoltage()/getChargerStatus()
    # disassembly and are now baked directly into hw_config.h Sec.9 as
    # BYOK_BATT_DIVIDER_RATIO_X1000 / BYOK_CHARGER_STAT_POLARITY -- no longer
    # a per-build guess, so removed from here.

    config BYOK_HW_LCD_FB_BIT_ORDER_LSB_TOP
        bool "Assume LCD framebuffer bit order is LSB = top row of the page"
        default y
        help
            hw_config.h Sec.13 BYOK_LCD_FB_BIT_ORDER: the framebuffer BYTE
            index is CONFIRMED ((y>>3)*240+x) but which bit within that byte
            is the panel's topmost row of its 8-row page is only STRONGLY
            INDICATED (the UC1611 family's usual RAM format), never actually
            observed on this panel. Leave this enabled (the documented best
            guess) until the display has been driven and a real image
            checked; disable it if the picture comes up vertically mirrored
            within each 8-row band.

endmenu
